{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Behold, seven years, etc.</b> He was precise in saying <b>in all the land of Egypt</b> twice, and did not say 'in the land' plainly as he said nearby — to say that the plenty is only in the land of Egypt, but the famine is throughout the entire world. Therefore, when he said ״וְכִלָּה הָרָעָב״ he did not say 'the land of Egypt' alone, but ״אֶת הָאָרֶץ״ — both the land of Egypt and the rest of the lands. And so it was, as it is written (Genesis 41:56): ״וְהָרָעָב הָיָה עַל כָּל פְּנֵי הָאָרֶץ״; and concerning the plenty Scripture said (Genesis 41:53): ״וַתִּכְלֶינָה שֶׁבַע שְׁנֵי הַשָּׂבָע אֲשֶׁר הָיָה בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״ — this tells us that there was plenty only in the land of Egypt, for otherwise there would have been no need to say ״אֲשֶׁר הָיָה בְּאֶרֶץ מִצְרָיִם״. And the making known of this matter to Joseph was from what he saw, that the cows were so exceedingly lean and ill-favored; from this he inferred that if there had been plenty in the world, they would not have been in Egypt in such a state of starvation during the seven years of famine, for they would bring bread from the other lands; but assuredly the famine is throughout the entire world, and in this there is no escape for them. But the plenty — there is nothing to prove that it would be in all the lands."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:38.485834291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}